    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d719">

                <pb facs="1004" n="888" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg888"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.512359 Shipping/14</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Danish Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Brun</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 236</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By my letter of August 12th (No.
                        230)<anchor n="3" xml:id="d719-f1"/> regarding an exchange of notes between
                    the Government of Denmark and the Government of the United States for the
                    reciprocal exemption of shipowners from income tax, I stated it to be the
                    understanding of the Danish Government that this exemption when established
                    would be as from January 1st 1921, notwithstanding the fact that the actual
                    exchange of notes can not be arranged for until some time hence <pb facs="1005"
                        n="889" xml:id="pg889"/> because the conditions stated in your note to me of
                    August 9th must first be brought to the knowledge of the Danish Government.</p>
                <p>I would be greatly obliged to you if you would be so good as to confirm to me the
                    correctness of the above named understanding.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. Brun</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
